# Arkiv × Puna Tech Hackathon — Cursor Rules

This repo contains official hackathon materials for the Arkiv × Puna Tech Hackathon, a hackathon track run by Arkiv at PunaTech in collaboration with Puna Tech / SaltaDev.

## Doc map
- What is the challenge? → README.md
- What should I build? → docs/builders-guide.md
- Install the Arkiv agent skill → docs/agent-skill.md
- Rules, prizes, eligibility → RULES.md
- How submissions are scored → docs/scoring-rubric.md
- Common questions → FAQ.md

## Key facts
- Prize: $1,500 USD total — 4 ranked prizes ($600 1st · $450 2nd · $300 3rd · $150 4th).
- Theme: AI apps on [ARKIV].
- Scoring: Arkiv integration depth 40%, functionality 30%, design/UX 20%, code quality 10%.
- All entities expire — use "expiration dates", never "TTL".
- Testnet: Arkiv Testnet (network ID: 60138453102).
- SDK: @arkiv-network/sdk@0.6.8.

## Testnet config
- HTTP RPC: https://braga.hoodi.arkiv.network/rpc
- WebSocket RPC: wss://braga.hoodi.arkiv.network/rpc/ws
- Standard Bridge: 0xB52b417A79c9dE21ffe221dF9a3821B7EaC60813
- Faucet: TBC — check Discord for updates

## Minimum requirements
- Define PROJECT_ATTRIBUTE — unique to your project. Stamp it on every entity and query. Without it, queries leak data from other projects.
- At least 2 entity types, related via shared-attribute foreign-key.
- Numeric attributes for range queries. String attributes for equality/glob. Never store a number as a string.
- Right-sized expiresIn per entity type using ExpirationTime helpers.
- Use $owner (mutable, controls write/update/delete) and $creator (immutable attribution) correctly.

## Language rules
- Say "Arkiv" — never "Golem Base".
- Say "expiration dates" — never "TTL".
- Say "tamper-proof" — never "verifiable".
- Avoid "trustless" and "fully decentralised" — Arkiv launches with centralised sequencers.

## Support
For Arkiv-specific issues: dedicated support channel (coming soon) on the Arkiv Discord (https://discord.gg/arkiv).
